    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 13th with a lineup anchored by the elite offensive potential of **Yordan Alvarez**, who leads the roster with an 85.83 efficiency score. His matchup against Miller, B (R) is exceptionally favorable, bolstered by a 0.423 xwOBA and a +17% SP Skill boost. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (79.70) remains our most vital strategic play today; while his batting order spot at #8 drags his score slightly, the combination of a weak opposing starter in Ritchie (R) and the massive +14% dynamic platoon advantage makes him a prime candidate to exploit the stolen base scarcity in our 5x5 format. Furthermore, **Kyle Schwarber** (62.66) receives a significant lift from the wind blowing out and a prime #1 spot in the order, effectively neutralizing a mediocre matchup against Gray, S (R).\n\nWhile the depth is reliable, the most difficult decision today involved the final utility spot. **Carson Benge** (42.46) narrowly secured the start over our other reserves. While **Lars Nootbaar**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena** were considered, the algorithm prioritized **Carson Benge**'s projected leading role in the lineup, despite his struggle against the handedness of Valdez, F (L). It was a tight call that necessitated looking past the platoon disadvantage to capture the extra plate appearance volume. Conversely, we remain cautious regarding **Dillon Dingler** (40.80); despite his #2 order spot, he faces an uphill battle against Scott (R), and his efficiency is hampered by a significant negative platoon adjustment. With **Trea Turner**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Hyeseong Kim** unavailable, and **Zac Veen** still developing in Albuquerque, we are relying on our core starters to maintain volume across the 5x5 categories without the safety net of our usual star-studded bench.",
